{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>Your little ones</b> — to teach that Israel should be in the eyes of the leaders like their own little ones, to guide them and lead them." "<b>Your women</b> — and adjacent to it: וגרך (and your stranger), a hint that they were not warned regarding the laws of kosher marriage to marry those disqualified."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {1 "כשרות here refers to the laws of permissible marriage (כשרות בנישואין), not dietary kashrut; the point is that women were not explicitly warned against marrying men who are halakhically disqualified."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:10:59.815644487Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}